cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "NeuroSpatialGradients: a calibrated spatial transcriptomics framework for the perineural microenvironment of triple-negative breast cancer"
authors:
  - family-names: "Lu"
    given-names: "Wenliang"
version: v1.0.0
date-released: "2026-11-12"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/luwen001199/neurospatial-gradients"
identifiers:/n  - type: doi
    value: "10.5281/zenodo.24165453"
    description: "Zenodo archive of release v1.0.0"
abstract: >-
  Quantifies the perineural microenvironment of triple-negative breast
  cancer from public 10x Visium data, with a two-stage statistical
  calibration (Moran spectral randomisation plus size-matched random
  gene sets) that corrects the false-discovery inflation caused by
  spatial autocorrelation and by gene-set size.
keywords:
  - spatial transcriptomics
  - perineural invasion
  - triple-negative breast cancer
  - Moran spectral randomisation
  - cancer-associated fibroblasts
